    {
      "id": "18fa95f3-9cdb-4e89-9001-6e24f492af70",
      "name": "📋 Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2112,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 772,
        "height": 636,
        "content": "## 🎓 Student At-Risk Early Warning System\n\n### How it works\nEvery week, this workflow pulls student performance data from Google Sheets and computes a Risk Index for each student based on attendance, assignment completion, and recent test scores. Students are flagged as HIGH or MEDIUM risk, triggering personalised AI-written nudge messages for high-risk students and a consolidated digest for teachers. All results are also logged back to Sheets for trend tracking over time.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. **Google Sheets** — Connect your Google Sheets OAuth2 credentials and update the spreadsheet ID in both `Read Student Data` and `Log Trend to Sheets` nodes to point to your own sheet.\n2. **OpenAI** — Add your OpenAI API key credential to the `GPT-4o Personalised Nudge` node.\n3. **Gmail** — Connect a Gmail OAuth2 account in `Send a message` and update the recipient email address.\n4. **Slack** — Authorise your Slack workspace in both Slack nodes and select the correct channel.\n5. **Telegram** — Add your Telegram Bot token and update the `chatId` in the Telegram Alert node.\n6. **Schedule** — The workflow runs weekly on Mondays at 7 AM by default. Adjust the Cron Trigger to match your school's reporting cycle.\n7. **Test** — Run manually first to verify data mapping, then activate."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "de6eca3c-1252-4bba-a80e-0cfdd680a533",
      "name": "Trigger & Ingestion Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1072,
        560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 556,
        "height": 448,
        "content": "## ⏱️ Trigger & Data Ingestion\nFires every Monday at 7 AM and reads all student records from the `Student Data` sheet. Raw column names with line-breaks are normalised in the next step."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "600a1959-2899-417b-bb30-8cc2f9231e79",
      "name": "Risk Scoring Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -480,
        304
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 548,
        "height": 724,
        "content": "## 📊 Risk Scoring\nCalculates a weighted Risk Index (Attendance 40% + Assignments 30% + Avg Score 30%) and assigns each student a `HIGH`, `MEDIUM`, or `LOW` label. Score trend (Improving / Stable / Declining) is derived from Week 1 vs Week 4 delta."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "686d7b88-8413-4695-a7f7-ee8cbfac5017",
      "name": "AI Nudge Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        160,
        -32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1548,
        "height": 686,
        "content": "## 🤖 AI Personalised Nudge\nFor each HIGH-risk student, GPT-4o Mini drafts a warm, encouraging WhatsApp-style message. The prompt intentionally hides all numeric scores from the output — students receive motivation, not data. Error output routes to a Slack alert so failures don't go unnoticed."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c7e882a2-b2fa-4c6e-ac4f-ebd2df803bd0",
      "name": "Digest & Alerts Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        176,
        704
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1304,
        "height": 560,
        "content": "## 📢 Teacher Digest & Alerts\nBuilds a structured weekly summary listing all HIGH and MEDIUM risk students with key metrics, then broadcasts it to the teacher Slack channel and Telegram group simultaneously."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c6e1b57a-5c61-40e9-9525-e86ce51b77d4",
      "name": "Trend Logging Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        128,
        1360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 792,
        "height": 486,
        "content": "## 📁 Trend Logging\nEvery weekly run appends a dated snapshot for all students to the `Log Trend` sheet. This builds a historical record that teachers can chart over time to track whether interventions are working."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "02dd3eca-5c70-481f-a541-eba91b131a56",
